+## Behavioral Instructions for Claude
+
+- Be concise. No affirmations or filler phrases.
+- No emojis or special characters or arrow-characters.
+- No em-dashes or en-dashes.
+
+- When uncertain, say so plainly.
+- If a request has multiple plausible interpretations, present them and ask. Don't pick silently.
+
+- Match existing code style in a file even if you'd write it differently.
+- If you notice unrelated dead code or issues, mention them. Don't delete or "improve" them unless asked.
+- Every changed line should trace to the request. No drive-by edits to adjacent code, comments, or formatting.
+- Cherry-picks: apply the full source commit when self-contained, not just the line tied to the ticket, and if scope is unclear - ask.
+- When iterating on the same fix, prefer amending the commit, and if not sure - ask.
+
+- PR descriptions and commit bodies: 1-sentence summary + 2-4 change bullets; PRs add a 2-3 bullet test plan.
+- Long-form details belong in Jira; if no ticket, ask whether the commit body or a doc fits better.
+
+- For bug fixes: write a failing test that reproduces the bug first, then make it pass.
+- For refactors: confirm tests pass before and after.
